{
  "name": "After the Storm: Steps for Major Roof Damage Assessment",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: Secure the Area and Document Initial Observations",
      "text": "Immediately after a major event, make sure the affected areas around your home are safe and prevent further damage if possible. Note the date and the suspected cause of the damage. From a safe distance, take photographs of any visible exterior and interior damage. This initial documentation is crucial for insurance purposes and helps create a baseline for a professional assessment.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: Conduct a Safe Exterior Visual Inspection",
      "text": "From the ground or a securely braced ladder, look for obvious signs of damage such as missing shingles, dents, punctures, or debris. Pay attention to roof slopes, flashing around chimneys and vents, and gutters. However, don't climb onto the roof if you're unsure of its stability or your safety. Professional roofers like Discounted Roofing Co. are trained to safely inspect even unstable roofs.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3: Inspect for Interior Damage",
      "text": "Move inside your home to check for any signs of water intrusion or structural issues. Look for water stains on ceilings and walls, peeling paint, or dampness. If you have attic access, safely check the attic space for leaks, damaged decking, or any compromise to structural elements. Even small leaks can indicate significant damage that needs attention.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4: Differentiate New Damage from Pre-Existing Wear",
      "text": "As you're assessing, try to distinguish between damage caused by the recent event and any older wear and tear. Older issues like faded shingles or minor scuffs might not be related to the recent storm. Professionals are skilled at identifying the exact cause of damage, which is vital for proper repair planning and insurance claims.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 5: Consult with a Professional Roofing Company",
      "text": "Once you’ve made your initial observations, it’s time to call in the experts. Discounted Roofing Co. offers free roof inspections and can provide a detailed assessment. They'll explain what they see, use photos for clear documentation, and help you understand whether the damage warrants an insurance claim or a straightforward repair. Their expertise in insurance claims restorations can guide you through the next steps. Taking these steps helps ensure your roof's major damage is thoroughly assessed, setting the stage for effective repairs and restoring your peace of mind. Need a professional major roof damage assessment? Contact Discounted Roofing Co. for a reliable inspection.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "speakable": {
    "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
    "cssSelector": [
      "h1",
      ".howto-step",
      "[itemprop=\"step\"]"
    ]
  },
